1
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:08,040
Expanding unpacks a bracket.

2
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:11,240
4, bracket, x plus 3, becomes 4 x plus 12.

3
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:13,520
Factorising does the opposite.

4
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:16,280
It packs the bracket back up.

5
00:00:16,330 --> 00:00:19,380
Can you write 6 y plus 15 with a bracket?

6
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:22,820
Pause the video and try it.

7
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:25,990
Find a number that divides both terms.

8
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:29,240
6 and 15 are both in the 3 times table.

9
00:00:29,290 --> 00:00:31,240
6 y divided by 3 is 2 y.

10
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:33,540
15 divided by 3 is 5.

11
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:37,440
So 6 y plus 15 equals 3, bracket, 2 y plus 5.

12
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:43,200
Check by expanding: 3 times 2 y is 6 y, and 3 times 5 is 15.

13
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:50,320
Remember: the highest common factor of two numbers is the biggest number that divides into both.

14
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:52,950
The H C F of 12 and 18 is 6.

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,210
The H C F of 20 and 35 is 5.

16
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:00,480
To factorise, find the highest common factor of all the terms.

17
00:01:00,530 --> 00:01:02,470
Write it outside the bracket.

18
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:05,500
Inside goes each term divided by it.

19
00:01:05,550 --> 00:01:07,890
The common factor can be a letter.

20
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:10,210
x squared and 4 x both contain x.

21
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:14,000
So x squared plus 4 x is x, bracket, x plus 4.

22
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:16,770
Or a number and a letter together.

23
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:19,440
10 A and 15 A B share 5 A.

24
00:01:19,490 --> 00:01:20,140
Your turn.

25
00:01:20,190 --> 00:01:22,180
Factorise x squared plus 4 x.

26
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:25,480
Pause the video and try it.

27
00:01:25,530 --> 00:01:26,950
Both terms contain x.

28
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,920
x squared divided by x is x.

29
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:30,470
4 x divided by x is 4.

30
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:33,470
The answer is x, bracket, x plus 4.

31
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:36,390
Always use the highest common factor.

32
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:39,770
12 x plus 18 equals 2, bracket, 6 x plus 9.

33
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:45,760
That is factorised, but not fully, because 6 x and 9 still share a 3.

34
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:48,080
The H C F of 12 and 18 is 6.

35
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:52,540
Fully factorised, it is 6, bracket, 2 x plus 3.

36
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:56,300
If one term is the H C F itself, a 1 is left inside.

37
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:59,370
5 x plus 5 is 5, bracket, x plus 1.

38
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:00,670
Here is the method.

39
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:03,810
Step 1: find the H C F of the numbers.

40
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:09,500
Step 2: find the letters that are in every term, with their lowest power.

41
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:11,710
Step 3: write the H C F outside.

42
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:15,230
Divide each term by it to fill the bracket.

43
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:21,730
Step 4: check by expanding, and check that nothing else is common inside the bracket.

44
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:24,060
Factorise 18 m minus 24.

45
00:02:24,110 --> 00:02:26,780
The H C F of 18 and 24 is 6.

46
00:02:26,830 --> 00:02:29,210
18 m divided by 6 is 3 m.

47
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:31,800
24 divided by 6 is 4.

48
00:02:31,850 --> 00:02:35,360
The answer is 6, bracket, 3 m minus 4.

49
00:02:35,410 --> 00:02:36,130
Your turn.

50
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:37,820
Factorise 9 A minus 9.

51
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:40,910
Pause and work it out.

52
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,090
The H C F is 9.

53
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:45,760
9 A divided by 9 is A, and 9 divided by 9 is 1.

54
00:02:45,810 --> 00:02:48,190
So it is 9, bracket, A minus 1.

55
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,220
Don't forget the 1.

56
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:53,060
Factorise 14 A B plus 21 A squared.

57
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:57,430
The H C F of 14 and 21 is 7, and both terms contain A.

58
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:59,600
So the H C F is 7 A.

59
00:02:59,650 --> 00:03:02,000
14 A B divided by 7 A is 2 B.

60
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:04,900
21 A squared divided by 7 A is 3 A.

61
00:03:04,950 --> 00:03:08,840
The answer is 7 A, bracket, 2 B plus 3 A.

62
00:03:08,890 --> 00:03:11,760
Factorise 6 x squared plus 9 x minus 3.

63
00:03:11,810 --> 00:03:12,880
The H C F is 3.

64
00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:17,170
It is not 3 x, because the last term, 3, has no x.

65
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:21,980
The answer is 3, bracket, 2 x squared plus 3 x minus 1.

66
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:24,870
Ava factorises 16 x minus 24 fully.

67
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:27,730
Which line goes wrong first?

68
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:29,040
Line 1 is wrong.

69
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:32,480
4 is a common factor, but not the highest.

70
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:34,610
4 x and 6 still share a 2.

71
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:37,450
The H C F of 16 and 24 is 8.

72
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:43,230
Fully factorised, 16 x minus 24 is 8, bracket, 2 x minus 3.

73
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,180
Factorising can save work.

74
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:49,160
A path is made of two rectangles, both 3 metres wide.

75
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:53,770
One is 17 metres long and the other is 13 metres long.

76
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:57,510
Instead of two calculations, take out the 3.

77
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:03,590
3, bracket, 17 plus 13, is 3 times 30, which is 90 square metres.

78
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:04,970
One last question.

79
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:07,420
Factorise 12 P Q plus 8 P fully.

80
00:04:07,470 --> 00:04:10,900
Pause the video and answer.

81
00:04:10,950 --> 00:04:15,050
The H C F of 12 and 8 is 4, and both terms contain P.

82
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,620
So the H C F is 4 P.

83
00:04:16,670 --> 00:04:18,900
12 P Q divided by 4 P is 3 Q.

84
00:04:18,950 --> 00:04:20,780
8 P divided by 4 P is 2.

85
00:04:20,830 --> 00:04:24,390
The answer is 4 P, bracket, 3 Q plus 2.

86
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:28,580
To remember: factorising is the reverse of expanding.

87
00:04:28,630 --> 00:04:33,070
Take out the highest common factor, numbers and letters.

88
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:36,780
Divide each term by the H C F to fill the bracket.

89
00:04:36,830 --> 00:04:41,350
Check by expanding, and check that nothing else is common.

90
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:46,550
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.4 on Camday.
